@page "/doctrine"
@attribute [BlazierPage("doctrine", Title = "Doctrine: an army game with a general that learns from you", Layout = typeof(MainLayout), Static = true)]
@implements IDisposable
@inject IBuildTime Build
@inject IJSRuntime JS
@inject IServiceProvider Services
@using ShowroomDoctrine
@using Doctrine

<PageTitle>Doctrine: an army game with a general that learns from you</PageTitle>

<div class="room dc @(_s is { InGame: true } ? "dc-ingame" : "")">
    @if (_s is not { InGame: true })
    {
        <header class="room-head">
            <nav class="crumb"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a> <span>/</span> Doctrine</nav>
            <h1>Doctrine</h1>
            <p class="lede">Draft an army from the companies the game offers, give it up to four orders from a council it lays out, and watch the battle run on a navigation mesh. Your general learns how you set
                orders from your own choices, in your browser, with nothing pre-trained, and suggests the next one. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
        </header>
    }

    @if (Build.IsPrerender)
    {
        <ToolStart Tool="Doctrine" Label="Start Doctrine" />
    }
    else if (_s is not null)
    {
        @if (!_s.InGame)
        {
            @if (_s.Notice.Length > 0) { <p class="dc-notice" role="status">@_s.Notice</p> }
            @if (_s.Error.Length > 0) { <p class="err" role="alert">@_s.Error</p> }
        }

        @switch (_s.Stage)
        {
            case DoctrineStage.Start:
                @StartView
                break;
            case DoctrineStage.Over:
                @OverView
                break;
            default:
                @Hud
                break;
        }
    }

    <section class="outro">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>Each round the game offers you a muster of companies of soldiers and, once you have drafted, a council of orders. You spend gold on the
            companies you want, may pay gold to draw the council again, give up to four of its orders (to a line, or to the whole host) and watch one battle. A battle is
            simulated once, on your device, and recorded. The replay is a recording of that one battle: playing it back does not run it again.</p>
        <details class="dc-about dc-built">
            <summary>How it is built</summary>
            <p>The army is a set of Pleroma stores from the Phasor package, the battle runs on a Tracer navigation mesh, the rounds run as EvalApp
                pipelines, and the general is @(DoctrineWords.GeneralBuilt(GeneralOpts)).</p>
            <p>Each cohort of soldiers is an item in a Pleroma store: its kind is the key, its traits are the flags, its place in the line is the
                arrangement, and its seasoning is a position on a ring of nine. An order is one operation on that store. Reforge relabels a trait,
                Reform the ranks relabels the line, Drill the host ticks the ring, Raise a banner counts the soldiers who carry a trait, and the list
                of orders you may give is read from the store, which is why some are greyed out. Orders for a line go to the battle: the ground is a
                baked Tracer navigation mesh, and each cohort is a group of agents that path, take cover and strike on it.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dc-about">
            <summary>About the general</summary>
            <p>Your general starts empty. It learns how you set a doctrine from your own choices, in your browser, with nothing pre-trained, and
                different players end up with different generals. It suggests and you decide: every doctrine you set is an example for it, and so is each
                battle result.</p>
            @foreach (var how in DoctrineWords.GeneralHow(GeneralOpts)) { <p class="dc-how">@how</p> }
            <p class="dc-howrecord">The match record is a score out of @DoctrineWords.RecordScale. @DoctrineWords.SlotRecordWords() For the whole pick it reads: @DoctrineWords.WholeRecordWords()</p>
            <p>Nothing is saved: refresh the page and the general is gone.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dc-about dc-rules">
            <summary>About the field</summary>
            <p class="dc-dugin-rule">@DoctrineWords.DugInRule()</p>
            <p class="dc-siege-rule">@DoctrineWords.SiegeRule(RoundChoices.Max())@(_s?.Grounds is { } grounds ? " " + DoctrineWords.SiegeGrounds(grounds) : "")</p>
            <p class="dc-limit-rule">@DoctrineWords.TickLimitRule()</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dc-about dc-warrules">
            <summary>About the war</summary>
            <p>A war is played in epochs. Each epoch you seal a pick of one road to push, or you hold back; the enemy picks its road without seeing yours, and both are shown together. If you both picked the same road, the two hosts meet in one battle on the ground of the province you assault, and the winner takes it. If you picked different roads, each side takes ground unopposed. A drawn battle moves nothing and costs nothing. A capital taken ends the war, and if both fall in one epoch it is a draw.</p>
            <p>A lost battle costs a standard, and winning battles raises them again, one at a time and never above the number you began with. With none left the war is lost. Holding back loses ground, never a standard.</p>
            <p>Every province you hold pays gold at the end of an epoch: open country the least, a province with a feature more, and the Granary the most. With no feature held the muster draws from @DoctrineWords.JoinAnd(UnlockPools.BaseKinds.Select(DoctrineWords.KindName).ToList()). @DoctrineWords.JoinAnd(new[] { Feature.Barracks, Feature.Stables, Feature.Shrine }.Select(f => DoctrineCampaignWords.FeatureName(f) + " adds " + DoctrineWords.JoinAnd(UnlockPools.KindsOf(f).Select(DoctrineWords.KindName).ToList())).ToList()), each for as long as you hold it; the Shrine also lets the council offer the order @DoctrineWords.ArmyTitle(ArmyOrderKind.Aura). A kind a feature opens is sold at the same price as any other, so it only widens the choice, and what you lose with a province leaves the next muster. The enemy's host on each road keeps its losses and musters back only a little each epoch.</p>
        </details>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    private enum Sheet { None, Army, General, Draft, Chronicle, Lanes }

    /// <summary>The lengths of game the start screen offers (the siege rule is said for the longest).</summary>
    private static readonly int[] RoundChoices = [3, 5, 8];

    /// <summary>The knobs of the general this page runs (the game's own default when the sections hold another kind), so the words follow what it does.</summary>
    private global::Doctrine.General.GeneralOptions GeneralOpts => (_s?.Sections.General as global::Doctrine.General.TinyHoloGeneral)?.Options ?? new global::Doctrine.General.GeneralOptions();

    private ReplayCursor? _cursor;          // the tick on screen, shared by the replay and the chronicle
    private Chronicle? _chron;              // the account of the battle on screen
    private RoundView? _chronFor;           // the round the account was built for

    private DoctrineSession? _s;
    private DoctrineProgress _p = new();
    private DoctrineStage _seen = DoctrineStage.Start;
    private int _seenTurn;

    // start screen
    private int _rounds = DoctrineSession.DefaultRounds;
    private string _seedText = "";
    private string _codeText = "";
    private string _loadError = "";

    // the scene
    private Sheet _sheet = Sheet.None;      // which panel is pulled up (phone); on a wide screen the panels are always there
    private bool _tray;                     // the order tray is open
    private UnlockNews? _news;              // what opened at the start of this round, until the player confirms it
    private string _advice = "";            // the game's advice line, while the draft or slots still hold exactly what it filled
    private int _lastAdded;                 // the order last put in a slot (its effect is previewed under the slots)

    // the muster: which of the offered companies are bought (parallel to the offer's packs), the line each would join and what the army says of it
    private bool[] _sel = [];
    private int[] _rank = [];
    private string?[] _packNote = [];
    private DraftPreview? _preview;
    private int _previewSeq;

    // the council
    private readonly int[] _slots = new int[DoctrineVocabulary.MaxSlots];
    private bool _ghostHidden;
    private int _dragFromSlot = -1;         // the slot being dragged to a new place in the order
    private string _formNote = "";          // why a formation could not be put in a slot

    private string _copied = "";

    // dragging a panel by its handle
    private double _dragFrom;
    private bool _dragged;

    /// <summary>The session behind the page (the proofs drive and read it).</summary>
    public DoctrineSession? Session => _s;
    /// <summary>What this visitor has unlocked (the proofs read it).</summary>
    public DoctrineProgress Progress => _p;

    private bool War => _s is { IsCampaign: true };
    /// <summary>In a war every kind and order is open to the page (the offer pool is the campaign's: what the held provinces open), so the ladder is at its top.</summary>
    private int Level => War ? DoctrineUnlocks.LastStep : _p.Step;
    private int SlotCount => DoctrineUnlocks.Slots(Level);
    private bool InDoctrine => _s?.Stage == DoctrineStage.Doctrine;
    /// <summary>The council is on the table and the visitor may put orders in the slots (not while the game is asking about a reroll, and not before the general has read it).</summary>
    private bool Choosing => _s is { Stage: DoctrineStage.Doctrine, Reroll: null };
    private bool Asking => _s is { Stage: DoctrineStage.Doctrine, Reroll: not null };

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (Build.IsPrerender) return;
        _p = Services.GetService(typeof(DoctrineProgress)) as DoctrineProgress ?? new DoctrineProgress();
        _s = new DoctrineSession(null, Services.GetService(typeof(DoctrineSectionsSource)) is DoctrineSectionsSource src ? src.Make : null, _p);
        _s.Changed += OnChanged;
    }

    private void OnChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(() =>
    {
        if (_s is null) return;
        if (_s.Stage != _seen || (_s.Turn != _seenTurn && _s.Stage is DoctrineStage.Draft or DoctrineStage.Doctrine)) { _seen = _s.Stage; _seenTurn = _s.Turn; EnterStage(_seen); }
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    private void EnterStage(DoctrineStage st)
    {
        _copied = "";
        _sheet = Sheet.None; _tray = false;
        if (st == DoctrineStage.Draft)
        {
            Array.Clear(_slots); _preview = null; _advice = ""; _lastAdded = 0;
            int packs = _s!.Draft?.Offer.Packs.Count ?? 0;
            _sel = new bool[packs]; _rank = Enumerable.Repeat(-1, packs).ToArray(); _packNote = new string?[packs];
            var news = War ? null : _p.Reach(_s.RoundIndex, _s.TotalRounds);
            if (news is not null) _news = news;
            _sheet = Sheet.Draft;
            _ = RefreshPreview();
        }
        if (st == DoctrineStage.Doctrine)
        {
            Array.Clear(_slots); _ghostHidden = false; _advice = ""; _lastAdded = 0; _formNote = "";
            if (_s!.Reroll is not null) { _sheet = Sheet.None; _tray = true; }
            else
            {
                bool ghost = _s.Ghost is { } g && !g.Doctrine.IsEmpty;
                _sheet = ghost ? Sheet.General : Sheet.None;
                _tray = !ghost;
            }
        }
        if (st is DoctrineStage.Start or DoctrineStage.Over) _news = null;
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (_s is null) return;
        _s.Changed -= OnChanged;
        _s.Dispose();
    }

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- start
    private RenderFragment StartView => @<div>
        <section class="dc-panel dc-start" id="dc-start" aria-label="Start a game">
            <h2>Start a game</h2>
            <p class="hint">Every game starts with an army levied for you, some gold to spend, and a run of rounds against armies the game raises. Each round you
                draft, set a doctrine, and watch one battle. Each round the game offers a muster of companies to buy and a council of orders to choose from. Round one offers two kinds of soldier and a few orders; more can be offered as the rounds go on.</p>
            <p class="dc-h3" id="dc-rounds-label">Rounds</p>
            <div class="dc-opts" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="dc-rounds-label">
                @foreach (var n in RoundChoices)
                {
                    var r = n;
                    <button type="button" class="dc-btn dc-opt @(_rounds == r ? "on" : "")" role="radio" aria-checked="@(_rounds == r ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => _rounds = r">@r rounds</button>
                }
            </div>
            <label class="dc-label" for="dc-seed">Game seed (optional)</label>
            <input id="dc-seed" class="dc-input" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false" maxlength="9"
                   placeholder="A whole number" value="@_seedText" @oninput="e => _seedText = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty" />
            <p class="hint">The same seed raises the same enemies on the same ground, so you can replay a game. Leave it empty for a new one.</p>
            <button type="button" class="dc-btn strong" id="dc-new" @onclick="StartNew">Start a new game</button>
            @if (Locked)
            {
                <button type="button" class="dc-btn dc-showall" id="dc-showall" @onclick="ShowEverything">Show everything</button>
            }
        </section>

        <section class="dc-panel dc-war" id="dc-war" aria-label="Start a war">
            <h2>Or fight a war</h2>
            <p class="hint">A war is fought over a map: your capital, the enemy's and @DoctrineWords.Cardinal(MapKeys.Lanes) roads of @DoctrineWords.Cardinal(MapKeys.StartLaneLength) provinces between them. Each epoch you seal a pick of the road to push; the enemy picks its road without seeing yours.
                The same road is a battle, different roads a race, and holding back costs ground but never a standard. Provinces you hold pay gold, and some open new soldiers and orders for as long as you hold them. A capital taken ends the war.</p>
            <p class="dc-h3" id="dc-mode-label">The war</p>
            <div class="dc-modes" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="dc-mode-label">
                <button type="button" class="dc-btn dc-mode @(!_endless ? "on" : "")" id="dc-mode-war" role="radio" aria-checked="@(!_endless ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => _endless = false">The war</button>
                <button type="button" class="dc-btn dc-mode @(_endless ? "on" : "")" id="dc-mode-endless" role="radio" aria-checked="@(_endless ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => _endless = true">Endless</button>
            </div>
            <p class="hint dc-modehint">@(_endless
                ? "Endless: the enemy has no capital. When you hold a whole road a fresh enemy province appears beyond it, and the enemy grows stronger every epoch. The run ends when your capital falls or you have no standards left. Your score is fields won plus provinces held."
                : $"The war: it ends when a capital falls, you have no standards left, or {DoctrineSession.WarEpochs} epochs have passed. Your score is fields won plus provinces held.") The seed above applies here too.</p>
            <button type="button" class="dc-btn strong" id="dc-campaign" @onclick="StartWar">@(_endless ? "Start the endless war" : "Start the war")</button>
        </section>

        <section class="dc-panel dc-load" aria-label="Load an army code">
            <h2>Load an army code</h2>
            <p class="hint">An army code is a short piece of text that holds an army. Paste one from an earlier game to play on with that army.</p>
            <label class="dc-label" for="dc-code">Army code</label>
            <textarea id="dc-code" class="dc-input dc-codebox" rows="3" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false"
                      placeholder="DA2.0...." @oninput="e => _codeText = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty">@_codeText</textarea>
            @if (_loadError.Length > 0) { <p class="err dc-loaderr" role="alert">@_loadError</p> }
            <button type="button" class="dc-btn" id="dc-load" @onclick="LoadCode">Load this army and play</button>
        </section>

        @if (_s!.Sections.General.ExamplesSeen > 0)
        {
            <section class="dc-panel" aria-label="Your general">
                <h2>Your general</h2>
                <p class="hint">It has seen @_s.Sections.General.ExamplesSeen @(_s.Sections.General.ExamplesSeen == 1 ? "example" : "examples") (each doctrine you set and each battle result) since you opened this page and will carry them into the next game. A refresh forgets them.</p>
                <button type="button" class="dc-btn" id="dc-resetgeneral" @onclick="ResetGeneral">Start with a new, empty general</button>
            </section>
        }
    </div>;

    private bool Locked => !War && !_p.ShowAll && _p.Step < DoctrineUnlocks.LastStep;

    private bool _endless;                  // the war option chosen on the start screen

    private void StartWar()
    {
        _loadError = "";
        int seed;
        if (_seedText.Trim().Length == 0) seed = (int)(Environment.TickCount64 & 0x7fffffff);
        else if (!int.TryParse(_seedText.Trim(), System.Globalization.NumberStyles.None, System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out seed))
        { _loadError = "A seed is a whole number, digits only."; return; }
        _news = null;
        _s!.NewCampaign(seed, _endless, out var why);
        if (why.Length > 0) _loadError = why;
    }
    private void ShowEverything() { _p.ShowEverything(); _news = null; }

    private void StartNew()
    {
        _loadError = "";
        int seed;
        if (_seedText.Trim().Length == 0) seed = (int)(Environment.TickCount64 & 0x7fffffff);
        else if (!int.TryParse(_seedText.Trim(), System.Globalization.NumberStyles.None, System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out seed))
        { _loadError = "A seed is a whole number, digits only."; return; }
        _news = null;
        _s!.NewGame(seed, _rounds, null, out var why);
        if (why.Length > 0) _loadError = why;
    }

    private void LoadCode()
    {
        _loadError = "";
        if (_codeText.Trim().Length == 0) { _loadError = "Paste an army code first."; return; }
        int seed = _seedText.Trim().Length > 0 && int.TryParse(_seedText.Trim(), System.Globalization.NumberStyles.None, System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var sd)
            ? sd : (int)(Environment.TickCount64 & 0x7fffffff);
        _news = null;
        if (!_s!.NewGame(seed, _rounds, _codeText, out var why)) _loadError = why;
    }

    private void ResetGeneral() => _s!.ResetGeneral();

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the scene
    private string Goal => War
        ? (_s!.Endless
            ? "Goal: hold the roads for as long as you can. The run ends when your capital falls or you have no standards left. Score is fields won plus provinces held."
            : $"Goal: take the enemy capital before yours falls, before you have no standards left, and within {_s!.TotalRounds} epochs.")
        : $"Goal: win as many of the {_s!.TotalRounds} {(_s.TotalRounds == 1 ? "field" : "fields")} as you can.";

    private CampaignGame Cw => _s!.Campaign!;
    /// <summary>The epoch on screen: the one just played on its summary, the one open otherwise.</summary>
    private int EpochShown => _s!.Stage == DoctrineStage.Epoch && _s.LastEpoch is { } le ? le.Epoch : _s.Briefing?.Epoch ?? _s.RoundIndex;
    private Func<int, ArenaInfo?> ArenaOf => i => _s?.Grounds is { Count: > 0 } g ? g[i % g.Count] : null;
    private int Income => _s!.Provinces.Where(p => p.Owner == Holder.Player).Sum(p => p.Yield);

    private string Todo()
    {
        var s = _s!;
        switch (s.Stage)
        {
            case DoctrineStage.Map:
                return "Pick a road to push, or hold back. Your pick is sealed against the enemy's.";
            case DoctrineStage.Epoch:
                return "Read what changed, then go on.";
            case DoctrineStage.Watch when War:
                return "Watch, read the recap, then press Continue.";
            case DoctrineStage.Draft:
                return s.RoundIndex == 0 && Level == 0
                    ? "Gold buys soldiers. Tap a company in the muster to buy it, then press Confirm."
                    : "Tap the companies you want from the muster, then press Confirm.";
            case DoctrineStage.Doctrine when s.Reroll is { } ask:
                return $"The council is drawn. Keep it, or pay {ask.Offer.RerollCost} gold to draw again.";
            case DoctrineStage.Doctrine:
                return $"Tap up to {SlotCount} {(SlotCount == 1 ? "order" : "orders")} from the council into the slots, then press GO."
                    + (s.Ghost is { } g && !g.Doctrine.IsEmpty ? " Your general has marked its pick of the council." : "");
            case DoctrineStage.Working:
                return s.Status.Length > 0 ? s.Status + "." : "Working.";
            case DoctrineStage.Watch:
                return "Watch, read the recap, then press Next round.";
            default:
                return "";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The account of the battle on the watch screen: built once per closed round, from its recording, and shared with the replay by one cursor.</summary>
    private void EnsureWatch()
    {
        if (_s is not { Stage: DoctrineStage.Watch, Last: { } v } || ReferenceEquals(_chronFor, v)) return;
        _chronFor = v;
        _cursor = new ReplayCursor();
        _chron = BattleChronicle.Build(v.Record.Replay, v.Record.PlayerDoctrine, _s.ArenaName(v.Record.ArenaId), DoctrineWords.KindName, v.TraitsOf, v.SiegeClock);
    }

    private RenderFragment Hud => @<div class="dc-hud" data-stage="@_s!.Stage.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" data-step="@Level">
        @{ EnsureWatch(); }
        <header class="dc-top" aria-label="Where the game stands">
            <ul class="dc-status dc-chips @(War ? "dc-warchips" : "")">
                @if (War)
                {
                    <li class="dc-c-epoch">Epoch @(EpochShown + 1)@(_s.Endless ? "" : $" of {_s.TotalRounds}")</li>
                    @if (_s.Army is { } wa) { <li class="dc-c-gold">Gold @wa.Gold</li> }
                    @if (_s.Campaign is not null)
                    {
                        <li class="dc-c-score">Score @Cw.Score</li>
                        <li class="dc-c-standards" aria-label="@DoctrineCampaignWords.StandardsWords(Cw.Standards, _s.MaxStandards, _s.Briefing?.WinsToRestore ?? _s.RestoreEvery, _s.RestoreEvery)">Standards @Pips()</li>
                    }
                }
                else
                {
                    <li>Round @(_s.RoundIndex + 1) of @_s.TotalRounds</li>
                    @if (_s.Army is { } a) { <li>Gold @a.Gold</li> }
                }
            </ul>
            <div class="dc-sheetbtns">
                <button type="button" id="dc-open-army" class="dc-btn dc-sheetbtn" aria-expanded="@(_sheet == Sheet.Army ? "true" : "false")" aria-controls="dc-army"
                        @onpointerdown="DragStart" @onpointerup="e => DragOpen(e, Sheet.Army)" @onclick="() => ToggleSheet(Sheet.Army)">Army</button>
                @if (_s.Stage == DoctrineStage.Map)
                {
                    <button type="button" id="dc-open-lanes" class="dc-btn dc-sheetbtn" aria-expanded="@(_sheet == Sheet.Lanes ? "true" : "false")" aria-controls="dc-lanes"
                            @onpointerdown="DragStart" @onpointerup="e => DragOpen(e, Sheet.Lanes)" @onclick="() => ToggleSheet(Sheet.Lanes)">Roads</button>
                }
                @if (_s.Stage is not (DoctrineStage.Watch or DoctrineStage.Map or DoctrineStage.Epoch))
                {
                    <button type="button" id="dc-open-general" class="dc-btn dc-sheetbtn" aria-expanded="@(_sheet == Sheet.General ? "true" : "false")" aria-controls="dc-general"
                            @onpointerdown="DragStart" @onpointerup="e => DragOpen(e, Sheet.General)" @onclick="() => ToggleSheet(Sheet.General)">General</button>
                }
                @if (_s.Stage == DoctrineStage.Watch && _chron is not null)
                {
                    <button type="button" id="dc-open-chronicle" class="dc-btn dc-sheetbtn" aria-expanded="@(_sheet == Sheet.Chronicle ? "true" : "false")" aria-controls="dc-chronicle"
                            @onpointerdown="DragStart" @onpointerup="e => DragOpen(e, Sheet.Chronicle)" @onclick="() => ToggleSheet(Sheet.Chronicle)">Chronicle</button>
                }
            </div>
            <p class="dc-goal">@Goal</p>
            @if (_s.Stage is DoctrineStage.Draft or DoctrineStage.Doctrine && _s.Ground is { } ground) { <p class="dc-groundline">@DoctrineWords.GroundBriefing(ground)</p> }
            <p class="dc-todo" role="status">@Todo()</p>
            @if (_s.Notice.Length > 0) { <p class="dc-notice" role="status">@_s.Notice</p> }
            @if (_s.Error.Length > 0) { <p class="err" role="alert">@_s.Error</p> }
        </header>

        <div class="dc-stage">
            @ArmySheet
            <section class="dc-field" aria-label="The field">
                @FieldView
            </section>
            @if (_s.Stage is not (DoctrineStage.Map or DoctrineStage.Epoch)) { @GeneralSheet }
            @if (_s.Stage == DoctrineStage.Map) { @LanePanel }
            @if (_s.Stage == DoctrineStage.Watch && _chron is not null) { @ChronicleSheet }
            @if (_s.Stage == DoctrineStage.Draft) { @DraftDrawer }
            @if (InDoctrine) { @Tray }
            @if (_news is { } news) { @UnlockCard(news) }
        </div>

        @Dock
    </div>;

    // ---- the army panel (left) ----
    private RenderFragment ArmySheet => @<aside id="dc-army" class="dc-sheet dc-armypanel @(_sheet == Sheet.Army ? "open" : "")" aria-label="Your army">
        @Grip("Army", CloseSheet)
        @if (_s!.Army is { } a)
        {
            <h2>Your army <span class="dc-sub">@a.Soldiers soldiers, @a.Gold gold</span></h2>
            @if (a.Cohorts.Count == 0) { <p class="hint">No cohorts.</p> }
            else
            {
                // Only the kinds that are open at this step are named; the rest wait under one collapsed line.
                var openRows = a.Cohorts.Where(c => DoctrineUnlocks.KindOpen(c.Key, Level)).ToList();
                var otherRows = a.Cohorts.Where(c => !DoctrineUnlocks.KindOpen(c.Key, Level)).ToList();
                if (openRows.Count > 0)
                {
                    <ul class="dc-cohortlist dc-army">
                        @foreach (var c in openRows) { @CohortRow(c) }
                    </ul>
                }
                if (otherRows.Count > 0)
                {
                    <details class="dc-other">
                        <summary>Other soldiers: @otherRows.Sum(c => c.Count)</summary>
                        <ul class="dc-cohortlist dc-army">
